---
// src/pages/privacy.astro

export const prerender = true;

import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { ORGANIZATION_ID, SITE_ORIGIN } from "@/utils/site/schema";

const title = "Privacy Policy - Sorted Tech";
const metaDescription =
  "Sorted Tech respects your privacy. Our policy details how we collect, use, and secure your information.";

const structuredData = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "WebPage",
  name: "Privacy Policy",
  description: metaDescription,
  url: `${SITE_ORIGIN}/privacy`,
  publisher: {
    "@id": ORGANIZATION_ID,
  },
};
---

<BaseLayout {title} {metaDescription} {structuredData}>
  <section class="content-card rounded-none">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>

    <p class="text-small mb-4">
      <strong>Effective Date:</strong> 10th October 2025.
    </p>

    <p class="mb-4 lg:mb-6">
      Your privacy is important to us. This policy explains how Sorted Tech
      collects, uses, and protects your information when you visit our website.
      By using our site, you agree to the terms outlined in this policy. If you
      do not agree, please refrain from using our site.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>
    <p>
      Sorted Tech does not actively collect personal data. However, certain
      information may be automatically collected through your interaction with
      the site, including:
    </p>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6">
      <li>
        <span class="text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200"
          ><strong>Personal Information:</strong></span
        >
        We collect personal details, such as your name or email address, only when
        you provide them (e.g., via contact forms or inquiries).
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200"
          ><strong>Automatically Collected Information:</strong></span
        >
        When you visit our site, general information such as your IP address, browser
        type, and usage data may be automatically collected for security, performance,
        and analytics purposes.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mb-4 lg:mb-6">
      We do not sell, rent, or share your personal data with third parties.
    </p>

    <h2>2. How We Use Your Information</h2>
    <p>We use the information we collect to:</p>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6">
      <li>Improve your experience on our website.</li>
      <li>Respond to inquiries or feedback you provide.</li>
      <li>Analyze website usage and optimize our content and performance.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mb-4 lg:mb-6">
      We do not use your personal information for any purposes other than those
      outlined in this policy.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Third-Party Services</h2>
    <p>
      We use third-party services to enhance your experience and improve our
      site's functionality. These services may collect certain data, such as:
    </p>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6">
      <li>
        <span class="text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200"
          ><strong>Cloudflare:</strong></span
        >
        For website security and performance optimization, Cloudflare may collect
        IP addresses, browser information, and cookies. For more details on Cloudflare's
        privacy practices, please refer to their
        <a
          href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="hover:underline">Privacy Policy</a
        >.
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200"
          ><strong>Google Analytics:</strong></span
        >
        We use Google Analytics to track user interaction with the site (e.g., pages
        visited, time spent on the site). Google Analytics uses cookies for this purpose.
        You can opt-out of Google Analytics tracking by using the
        <a
          href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="hover:underline">Google Analytics Opt-Out Browser Add-On</a
        >.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mb-4 lg:mb-6">
      For more information about how these services handle your data, please
      check their respective privacy policies.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Cookies and Tracking Technologies</h2>
    <p>
      We use cookies to enhance your experience and to help us understand how
      users interact with the site. Cookies are small text files stored on your
      device, and they allow us to analyze website traffic, track user
      preferences, and improve site functionality.
    </p>
    <ul class="mb-6 list-disc pl-6 lg:mb-8">
      <li>
        <span class="text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200"
          ><strong>What cookies we use:</strong></span
        >
        Performance cookies (for anonymous data on site usage) and security cookies
        (for site protection).
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200"
          ><strong>Why we use cookies:</strong></span
        >
        Cookies help us improve your browsing experience, optimize content, and ensure
        the site runs smoothly.
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200"
          ><strong>Who provides these cookies:</strong></span
        >
        Third-party providers, such as Google (via Google Analytics) and Cloudflare
        (for security and performance), may set cookies on your behalf.
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200"
          ><strong>How you can manage cookies:</strong></span
        >
        You can control cookie preferences directly in your browser settings. Most
        browsers allow you to refuse or delete cookies. However, disabling cookies
        may affect your user experience and certain features of the site.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>5. Data Security</h2>
    <p class="mb-4 lg:mb-6">
      We take reasonable precautions to protect your information from
      unauthorized access, alteration, or disclosure. However, no data
      transmission over the internet is 100% secure, and we cannot guarantee
      absolute security.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Your Rights</h2>
    <p>
      Depending on where you live, you may have certain rights regarding your
      personal data. These include:
    </p>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6">
      <li>The right to access personal data we have collected about you.</li>
      <li>The right to request corrections or deletions of your data.</li>
      <li>The right to object to certain processing activities.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mb-4 lg:mb-6">
      Since Sorted Tech does not actively collect personal data, there may be no
      data for us to provide, correct, or delete. If you believe we hold any
      personal data about you or have any other concerns, please don't hesitate
      to contact us.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Changes to This Policy</h2>
    <p class="mb-4 lg:mb-6">
      We may update this Privacy Policy periodically to reflect changes in our
      practices or legal obligations. When significant changes are made, we will
      notify you with a prominent notice on our website.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Contact Information</h2>
    <p class="mb-4 lg:mb-6">
      If you have any questions or concerns about this Privacy Policy, please
      reach out to us through our <a href="/contact" class="hover:underline"
        >Contact</a
      > page.
    </p>
    <p>
      We value your privacy and are committed to being transparent about how we
      handle your information. Thank you for visiting Sorted Tech.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
